  "raw": " be required for all tracks.\n\nThe new electric day-to-day transport has been designed by the UKs Rolls-Royce and is following a blueprint from SAIC Motor about how to make hydrogen cars more practical for everyday use.\n\nThe technology would also be potentially useful for public transport and the UK Government also funds research in the technology at least partially. However, the realistic use for hydrogen in heavy industry isn't really known as of yet.\n\nThe technology has been shown to be capable of producing power without a tailpipe denting emissions with a preliminary estimate generating 0.026grams of CO2 from three nearby electric cars.\n\nRolls plans to sell the car through its discount brand - mixing a number of electric, diesel and plug-in hybrid cars - by 2020. Canada and Singapore are the primary markets and customers are expected to be in the same price range as combustion engine cars.\n\nIt will therefore need a production base for high volume on the",
